WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.167
-It's always great
to see you, bud.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.701
-Buddy, good to see you.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:04.834
Good to see y'all.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.334
-I mean, come on,
that's pretty good, right?

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:08.501
-Come on. Come on.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.834
Good to see the Roots.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:12.267
-Yeah, that's right, the Roots
right there, come on.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.634
Season finale of
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.067
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yes.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.100
It's a big show, Natasha Lyonne.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.100
Or White Whoopi,
as I like to call her.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.033
[ Laughter ]
-You call -- White Whoopi?

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.367
-Yeah, she's got
that gravelly --

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.133
You ever heard her talk?
-Yeah.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.334
-Oh, and she's very New York.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:27.467
She sounds like Whoopi.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.234
-You think she's sounds like
Whoopi Goldberg?

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:32.567
She's such a funny person,
I know a giant fan of the show,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.834
so I think her hosting --
she's like, freaking out.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.367
-She's the best.
-It's gonna be fun, yeah, yeah.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.834
-It's gonna be a great show.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:41.400
-You've reached an incredible
stat that I read recently.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.567
Is it 1,500 sketches
that you've been in?

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:46.934
-Yes.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.534
-1,500?

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.601
1,500 sketches.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.701
-1,500!

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.434
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.334
It seems like a lot.
-It does.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.234
It is a lot.
It definitely is a lot.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.534
I mean, that's wild.

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:04.634
Did you know going into the show
that you'd hit that mark?

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.267
-Only that day.
Like, somebody posted like,

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.767
"Kenan Thompson is only
3 sketches away from 1,500."

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.000
I was like, "Really?
Like, that's crazy.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.834
I missed all 1,490 --"
I wasn't counting.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.801
-Yeah, no one was counting.
Yeah, but that's wild.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:20.434
-But yeah, and then I saw that
I had four sketches that day.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.501
And then at the dress rehearsal
they were all in, so I was like,

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.834
"Oh, snap, I'm going to, like,
do this tonight, basically."

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.567
So I had that moment of like,
"That's pretty cool."

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.667
And then after I -- I didn't
think anybody was going to be,

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.567
like, waiting to celebrate it
necessarily but, you know,

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:36.133
our tender staff and crew were
back there with, like,

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.067
a card
and they were all clapping.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.334
-"SNL"?
-It was a nice moment.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.567
-Nah, come on, buddy, that's
great. I'm so happy.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.801
-Couldn't happen to
a better guy.

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:50.067
Do you know what to do now
in a sketch, like, when you have

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:53.367
a line and it just bombs,
and it just gets no laughs?

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:56.167
-I do now. Kind of like
that Whoopi joke earlier.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:02:00.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.567
Yeah, I just laugh through it
and go with it.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:06.767
But my first experience with
that was not great, necessarily.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.167
It was, like, the first time --
-Do you remember it?

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:12.334
-Yeah. It was the first time a
writer, like, wrote me a sketch

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.801
where I was, like,
a leading person.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:17.467
And it was called
"Randy the Bellhop."

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.167
-Hold your applause.
-You know what I'm saying?

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.467
[ Laughter ]
Relax.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.467
-"Do Randy, man!"
-You know what I'm saying?

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.267
"Do that Randy, man.
We don't want to hear that --"

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:31.234
So, it's called
"Randy the Bellhop."

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.934
I was a bellhop doing
shenanigans whatever,
checking in people.

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:37.567
Anyway, I flubbed a line,
like, really, really hard.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.701
I stumbled over it,
and I just let it be quiet.

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:42.667
I was just like -- I didn't try
to fix it or anything.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.334
I didn't try to laugh through it
or nothing.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.133
I didn't have the confidence
to, like, continue.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.801
I just let the moment,
like, hit the floor.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.267
-And just froze?
-And it was very, very quiet.

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.400
And I heard
this one lady go, "Aww."

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.634
-Oh, that's bad.
-You know what I mean?

00:02:58.634 --> 00:02:59.701
-"Aww."

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.334
-I didn't even react to that.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.133
-I was so green.
I was just like,

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.767
"Yeah, this is not going to --"
I finished the sketch

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.634
or whatever, and they didn't
write for me much after that.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:08.901
It's fine.
-It makes you feel like you're

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.300
letting them down, you know,
when you're doing --

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.634
when the writer writes something
for you.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.601
You're so honored
that they wrote for you.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.267
-1,000%. I was so nervous,
you know what I mean?

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.067
And I was just shaky
and blah blah blah.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:21.968
But now I just -- I really enjoy
when things go off-rail.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.567
-Yeah, it's just
a little different.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:24.901
-It's kind of the best.
-Yeah.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.567
[ Laughter ]
If something just sits here

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.200
and just tanks, you just kind of
go like --

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.167
-It pumps me up.
Like, I want to get crazy and,

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:31.534
like, start running through
the audience or something

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:32.968
if a joke doesn't work.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.300
It's like,
"Oh, y'all don't like that?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.033
Well, how do you like this?"
-Yeah!

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.234
Can you clear something up here?
'Cause I --

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.200
Samuel L. Jackson recently said

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.534
that you got him
banned from "SNL."

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:44.834
Do you know what
he's talking about?

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.033
-I don't have the authority
to do that.

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:49.334
I don't know why he thinks that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:51.968
But, no, I --
This is a great story.

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:53.868
Which camera am I on?
-You can go to one.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.834
-Hey, Sam.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.267
It's all good, bro.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.801
You're welcome any time,
from what I've been hearing.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:04.100
Anyway, he dropped the F bomb
on the show, but he says

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.000
I was supposed to cut him off
before that.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.400
But the cue card, it was just
an F on the cue card.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.434
It wasn't, like, the whole word.
-Oh, yeah, no other letters.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:12.234
-I was thinking he was just
gonna go, like, a fake move

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.667
and stop at the "f-,"
you know what I mean?

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.934
-Of course. "What the f-"
-But he went full train at it

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.467
because, you know, I guess
he's a method kind of guy.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:19.667
-Exactly, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.067
A method guy.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.901
-So when he did it the first --
He did it twice!

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.434
When he did it the first time,
I was processing like,

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:27.734
"Oh, snap, he did it and I
didn't make it," or whatever.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.634
"I didn't cut him off in time."
-'Cause you're live.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.934
-I was like "Okay, whatever,
that was pretty cool, but we

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:34.868
kind of expect the F word of
Sam Jackson, so no harm done."

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:36.000
-Yeah, every time he's on,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.868
we know that that's probably
going to happen.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:40.434
-Yeah. But then he doubled down
and said it again, I was like,

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:41.601
"Yo, my man,
we gotta pay for those,

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.234
you know what I'm saying?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:44.868
And it got a reaction...
-A lot of money, yeah, yeah.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.734
-...and we were able to,
like, get out of the moment.

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:49.234
Yeah, but he was -- he's been
mad at me for that.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.067
So, my bad, bro.
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.834
I didn't think he was gonna do
it like that.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.801
-No, no, he doesn't get mad.
-Come on in whenever you want.

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.100
-He's the greatest.
-It's Sam Jackson.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.501
Who doesn't want Sam Jackson on?
-Sam Jackson, come on.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.501
Yeah, you can host "The Tonight
Show" if you want, Sam.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:01.601
-Right, you heard it.
-Yeah, come on, bud.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.334
We love you, yeah.
-You heard it here.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.133
-I love your impressions.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.567
I like David Ortiz, "Big Papi."

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.400
-Oh, he's the best.
-When you do that.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.801
-He's the best.
-Yeah, I mean that, yeah.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.968
[ Laughter ]
-He's the best.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.300
-You got to meet him.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. I love him.

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.200
-What does he think of
the impression?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.267
-You know, it was my chance to
do, like, a Scarface impression,

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:23.934
you know what I mean?
When I heard that, you know --

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:26.067
"Big Papi" talk like that,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.367
[ as Ortiz ]
I can actually do it, man,
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.968
Take my Tony Montana moment.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.000
You know what I'm saying?"
-"That's how you do it."

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.634
-"Talk about the Red Sox."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.634
"Maybe talk about --
talk about Miami a little bit."

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.968
-[ as Ortiz ] "A little bit."

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.334
-[ Normal voice ]
He's just such a jolly person.

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:45.167
It allows for me to have
that fun like that.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.734
And, yeah, I met him, I did
his podcast, and he was like,

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:49.067
[as Ortiz]
"Yo, my man, I knew I made it

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:50.534
when you was doing me
on the show."

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.467
[ Normal voice ]
I love that guy.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.834
Big Papi. Big lunch.
-He's the best, man.

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:59.734
-He likes to have a big lunch.
-I love that guy.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:03.167
I know you just started
this production company.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.667
-Yeah, shout-out.
-And this is a big deal, bud.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:07.067
-Yeah, shout-out to Artists for
Artists, thank you very much.

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:08.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.400
-This is the chapter --
This is what you dream of.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.567
-I feel like this is
the next stage in life.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:17.033
So I partnered with my buddy
Johnny Ryan.

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:20.200
And we started this thing
where it's going to allow for

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.367
lots of things to come under it,
and, uh --

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:23.901
-It's called
Artists for Artists?

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:27.534
-Artists for Artists because we
believe in artists being able

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:30.634
to have some ownership kind of
in what they do,

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:32.300
you know what I mean,
so even if it has to come out

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.901
of our portion or our proceeds,
we want to make sure that,

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:37.234
you know, anybody that does
a movie should be able to get

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.300
a percentage of that movie
for as long as it's out,

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.000
you know what I mean?
Not just being paid to show up

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.901
and do the work, you should have
participation as it goes along.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:48.133
Like, imagine if you had
participation in "Beetlejuice."

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:51.234
Just take that, for example,
a 40-year-old idea or whatever

00:06:51.234 --> 00:06:53.434
and you have a percentage of
that, that's way better

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:56.367
than just getting whatever check
they gave him in 1988.

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:58.000
You know what I'm saying?
-Exactly. Yeah, right.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.067
-That's kind of
the strategy of it.

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:02.367
But also it's gonna be
the mothership.

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:03.667
It's gonna allow for
a lot of other things --

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:05.267
-You're doing documentaries,
you're doing --

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:07.167
-Docs, movies, a lot of stuff

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.701
that I don't necessarily
have to be at to happen.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.267
-But you're doing
a live thing too.

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.467
What are you doing with
Mike Tyson?

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:14.734
-Yeah, we have, you know,
a live element too.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.334
'Cause we're big Broadway fans,
me and my partner.

00:07:17.334 --> 00:07:19.634
And, you know, we're fans of
everything first, kind of,

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:22.567
so we're launching with Tyson
coming back to the stage with

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:24.868
"Undisputed Truth 2."

00:07:24.868 --> 00:07:27.367
He did his one-man show
back in the day.

00:07:27.367 --> 00:07:29.467
I think Spike was directing it.
-Yeah.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.801
-This is part two.
So we're starting with that

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:33.934
and other stuff like that.
-How'd you meet Mike?

00:07:33.934 --> 00:07:37.133
-I met Mike -- He did a "What's
Up With That?" back in the day,

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:38.868
actually, and he was --
-Oh, did he really?

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:40.467
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
He was very funny.

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.334
He got up and like,
you know, turned around

00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:43.601
and, like, shook his butt
in the camera.

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:44.801
[ Laughter ]
Stuff like that.

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:46.868
-All the stuff couldn't happen
to a better guy.

00:07:46.868 --> 00:07:49.100
Congrats on the season finale
of "SNL."

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.234
Kenan Thompson right here,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:52.234
-Thank you, man.
-The one and only.

00:07:52.234 --> 00:07:54.734
The season finale of "Saturday
Night Live" is this weekend

00:07:54.734 --> 00:07:56.300
with host Natasha Lyonne

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.133
and musical guest
Japanese Breakfast.

